446 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 219 0 R
/E (In the internal test, the best model is EfficientNetB5 \(94.4%\), closely followed by EfficientNetB0 \(94.1%\) and DenseNet121 \(93.0%\). However, in external validation, DenseNet121 generalizes best. A possible reason is model complexity: DenseNet121 has far fewer parameters than EfficientNetB5, so it may be less prone to learning dataset-specific patterns and more robust under domain shift. This shows that the best internal performance does not always guarantee the best external robustness.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
